  "body": "**Found by:** the second review of PR #2659 (comment 6997335188, point F2). Related: #2597.\n\n**What happens:** `FRESH_HALF_WIDTH` lets a strip of less than 0.05 mm stand up to Top Z for each band. On a slow chamfer, these strips are cut at the full height with a very small radial engagement.\n\nThe reviewer thinks that this is probably acceptable. It is not written down for the user.\n\n**Wanted:**\n- Measure the largest strip height and width on a slow chamfer with a headless test.\n- If the cut is acceptable, name it in the user note or in the documentation.\n- If it is not acceptable, make the strip step down as the other new outlines do.\n\n**Done means:** a test pins the measured strip, and the note or the documentation names it.\n",
